lowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-17T22:58:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T20:33:42Z","body":"- Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100980.\n\nWhat are you using to measure CPU utilization? The Windows task manager divides the displayed percentage by the CPU thread count, so it will look very low even if one CPU thread is being fully utilized.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2664196581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2664904218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102914#issuecomment-2664904218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102914","id":2664904218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6e1zYa","user":{"login":"agorangetek","id":53648632,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNjQ4NjMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53648632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek","html_url":"https://github.com/agorangetek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T08:18:13Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T08:18:13Z","body":"@Calinou Yes i am using task manager. I am looking at the overall CPU usage for the app regardless of the cores it's using. I brought this up because i notice my laptop fans working more frequently compared to 4.3. Regardless, CPU usage is higher for the same project.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2664904218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2665471851","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102914#issuecomment-2665471851","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102914","id":2665471851,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6e399r","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T11:56:39Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T11:56:39Z","body":"I think this regression is introduced in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99833, on my computer delay 10000 usecs result in sleeping 8000 usecs and spinning 2000 usecs, which cause a 1%-2% CPU usage. Profile shows we spent 99% of the time in this loop:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/93d270693079ea7802c9e1334a2e0ecd8529eeed/platform/windows/os_windows.cpp#L2340C3-L2342C4\n\nI think we should reconsidering where to apply this new delay algorithm, as it has a major flaw: it causes consistently high CPU usage for certain given delay durations (you can always construct such a value, currently 1000~10000 I think), which seems unacceptable for laptops and mobile platforms. Perhaps a toggle should be provided to allow users to choose the old algorithm.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2665471851/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2666877244","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102914#issuecomment-2666877244","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102914","id":2666877244,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6e9VE8","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T20:36:07Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T20:36:52Z","body":"This would probably be significantly improved by https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11099 (without having to compromise on frame pacing). However, I still don't know if the proposed instruction has an Intel equivalent.\n\n> Perhaps a toggle should be provided to allow users to choose the old algorithm.\n\nI suppose low processor usage mode should keep using the old sleep approach, while the FPS cap (`Engine.max_fps`) should keep using the new approach. This way, games keep having good frame pacing, while non-game applications favor low power consumption at the cost of frame pacing.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2666877244/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667707595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102914#issuecomment-2667707595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102914","id":2667707595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fAfzL","user":{"login":"agorangetek","id":53648632,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNjQ4NjMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53648632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek","html_url":"https://github.com/agorangetek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agorangetek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-19T07:19:55Z","updated_at":"2025-02-19T07:19:55Z","body":"> I suppose low processor usage mode should keep using the old sleep approach, while the FPS cap (`Engine.max_fps`) should keep using the new approach. This way, games keep having good frame pacing, while non-game applications favor low power consumption at the cost of frame pacing.\n\nI think this is the perfect solution as using low processor usage mode probably means the user is not making a game although static games could also benefit.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667707595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/270709616